statement='''Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space, including dimension zero, with its Borel measurable structure. Let V:E→ℝ be C². Let α,β be nonnegative reals and η a real number satisfying α>0, α≤β, α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v∈E, η>0, and βη≤1. Fix any y,xRef∈E and initial phase z0=(x0,p0)∈E×E. Set c=y−η∇V(xRef). For z=(x,p), define the actual harmonic flow Φ_t(z)=(c+cos(t)(x−c)+√η sin(t)p, −sin(t)(x−c)/√η+cos(t)p), reflection S(z)=(x,p−[2〈p,g(x)〉/‖g(x)‖²]g(x)), residual g(x)=∇V(x)−∇V(xRef), and rate λ(z)=√η max{0,〈p,g(x)〉}. The reflection uses total real division, hence is the identity when g(x)=0. Define Λ(z,t)=∫_0^t λ(Φ_s(z)) ds for finite t≥0 and τ(z,e)=inf{t≥0:Λ(z,t)≥e}, with inf empty=∞. Let P be the actual countable product of rate-one exponential Borel measures on Ω=ℝ^ℕ; let ε_k(sample)=max{sample_k,0} viewed as a nonnegative real. Define active records (T,z) and an absorbing stopped record carrying no phase. Initialize record0=(0,z0). At index k, a stopped record stays stopped; an active record (T,z) becomes stopped if τ(z,ε_k)=∞ and otherwise becomes (T+τ(z,ε_k), S(Φ_{τ(z,ε_k)}(z))). Its event time T_k is the finite time component if active and ∞ if stopped. Then for these fixed y,xRef,z0, for P-almost every sample, simultaneously: (i) for every finite nonnegative physical time t there exists exactly one n∈ℕ with T_n≤t<T_(n+1); (ii) for every such t and every index n satisfying those inequalities, there exists exactly one finite live record a=(s,z) such that record_n=inl(a), s≤t, and t−s<τ(z,ε_n), using nonnegative real subtraction and extended-valued comparison. In particular no stopped record supplies a phase, and when the next wait is infinite the last live record continues to cover every later finite physical time. Initialization index0 is retained and ε_n is source E_(n+1). Half-open intervals fix event-endpoint ownership; zero-length intervals are empty and strict positive waits are not an extra premise. This is the ASTIS interval/live-record/elapsed adapter needed by Appendix A.1's between-jump formula. It does not construct a global interpolated process, assert index(t=0)=0, or prove measurability, path regularity, full process uniqueness, Markov/invariance or costs.'''
assumptions=[
 'E is finite-dimensional real inner-product with its Borel measurable structure; no positive-dimension restriction. V is C² and α,β≥0.',
 'The six exact source conditions are α>0; α≤β; V∈C²; for all x,v, α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖²; η>0; βη≤1. No third or higher derivative condition.',
 'y,xRef,z0 are arbitrary deterministic parameters. P and ε are literal canonical definitions. No probability, iid, positivity, divergence, cap, energy, waiting-time or recurrence certificate is a public premise.',
 'Threshold positivity and faithful clamp/raw equality hold simultaneously only almost surely. The all-finite-horizon conclusion is pathwise on the common good-input event for each fixed parameter triple; no uncountable intersection over triples is assumed.',
 'Stopped records have eventTime=∞ and carry no phase. Every selected record is live with finite stored time and finite nonnegative elapsed offset. The next wait may be infinite; zero-length intervals are empty. No positive-wait, index, recurrence, nonaccumulation, measurable-selector or path certificate is a public premise.'
]
formulas=[r'c=y-\eta\nabla V(x_{\rm ref}),\quad g(x)=\nabla V(x)-\nabla V(x_{\rm ref}),\quad\lambda(x,p)=\sqrt\eta\max\{0,\langle p,g(x)\rangle\}.',r'\Phi_t(x,p)=\left(c+\cos t(x-c)+\sqrt\eta\sin t\,p,\ -\frac{\sin t}{\sqrt\eta}(x-c)+\cos t\,p\right),\quad S(x,p)=\left(x,p-\frac{2\langle p,g(x)\rangle}{\|g(x)\|^2}g(x)\right).',r'\Lambda(z,t)=\int_0^t\lambda(\Phi_s z)\,ds,\quad\tau(z,e)=\inf\{t\ge0:\Lambda(z,t)\ge e\},\quad\inf\varnothing=\infty.',r'P\text{-a.s.}:\quad\forall t\in[0,\infty),\quad\exists!n\in\mathbb N:\ T_n\le t<T_{n+1};\quad\operatorname{record}_n=(s,z),\quad s\le t,\quad t-s<\tau(z,\varepsilon_n).']
s=raw.decode(); body=s.index(':= by\n',s.index('theorem actual_fixed_reference_physical_time_cover'))+len(':= by\n')
def step(title,text,formula,start,end):
 a=s.index(start,body);b=s.index(end,a);code=s[a:b].rstrip()+'\n'
 return dict(title=title,text=text,formula=formula,lean=code,detail='Exact contiguous compiled proof region; preceding local definitions and facts remain in scope.',lean_source_region=dict(path=file,source_raw_sha256=sha(raw),start_line=s[:a].count('\n')+1,end_line=s[:a+len(code)].count('\n'),exact_code_raw_sha256=sha(code.encode())))
steps=[
 step('Fix the actual source objects and finite-time target','Keep the literal source flow, reflection, hazard, first hitting time and guarded finite-record recurrence. Use the canonical Exp1 product and total NNReal thresholds. The two conclusions concern the actual half-open clock interval and the actual stored live record with finite elapsed time.',r'T_n=\operatorname{time}(\operatorname{record}_n),\quad T_n=\infty\text{ if stopped};\quad T_n\le t<T_{n+1}.','  classical\n','  -- Exact deterministic'),
 step('Reuse initialized monotone actual clocks on the common AE event','The exact finite-recursion parent supplies initialization, monotonicity and guarded next-record updates. The actual nonaccumulation parent supplies finite-horizon escape on one AE event for each fixed parameter triple. No certificate is supplied as a new public assumption.',r'T_0=0,\quad T_n\le T_{n+1},\quad\forall t<\infty,\quad T_n>t\text{ eventually}.','  -- Exact deterministic','  · -- The first clock'),
 step('Select the predecessor of the first clock crossing','For each finite t choose the least k with t<T_k. Initialization gives k>0. Let n=k−1. Minimality gives T_n≤t, and n+1=k gives t<T_(n+1).',r'k=\min\{j:t<T_j\}>0,\quad n=k-1,\quad T_n\le t<T_{n+1}.','  · -- The first clock','    -- Monotonicity'),
 step('Prove that the half-open interval index is unique','If two indices m,n satisfy their half-open inequalities, m>n would imply T_(n+1)≤T_m≤t, contradicting t<T_(n+1). The opposite inequality is symmetric. Empty zero-length intervals cause no overlap, so no extra strict-wait premise is needed.',r'm>n\Longrightarrow t<T_{n+1}\le T_m\le t,\quad\text{a contradiction}.','    -- Monotonicity','  · -- A clock'),
 step('Exclude stopped records at finite covering times','A stopped record has eventTime=∞. Its lower interval inequality ∞≤t contradicts finiteness of t. Thus every covering record must be active.',r'T_n\le t<\infty\Longrightarrow\operatorname{record}_n\ne\mathrm{stopped}.','  · -- A clock','    | inl a =>'),
 step('Recover the actual live record and its stored time','For an active record a the exact eventTime eliminator gives T_n=a.time. The lower interval inequality gives a.time≤t. The record supplied in the conclusion is this actual record, not a chosen external state.',r'\operatorname{record}_n=\mathrm{inl}(a)\Longrightarrow T_n=a.time\le t.','    | inl a =>','      · -- Infinite wait'),
 step('Keep the last live arc when the next wait is infinite','If the actual next waiting time is infinity, every finite NNReal elapsed offset is strictly less than it. Stopping the next jump does not erase the currently live state or invent a phase at infinity.',r'\tau(a.state,\varepsilon_n)=\infty\Longrightarrow t-a.time<\infty=\tau(a.state,\varepsilon_n).','      · -- Infinite wait','        -- Finite wait:'),
 step('Bound the elapsed offset for a finite next wait','Write the actual finite wait as q. The existing guarded recurrence gives record_(n+1)=(a.time+q, bounce(flow(q,a.state))) and hence T_(n+1)=a.time+q. Therefore t<T_(n+1) and a.time≤t imply t−a.time<q. Subtraction is nonnegative and never evaluates an infinite elapsed duration.',r'T_{n+1}=a.time+q,\quad a.time\le t<T_{n+1}\Longrightarrow 0\le t-a.time<q.','        -- Finite wait:','      · -- The stored record'),
 step('Prove uniqueness of the actual live record','The record recursion is a function. Two live records at the same index have equal Sum.inl values, so injectivity gives equal time/state pairs. Assemble the interval and live-record conclusions on the common AE event.',r'\mathrm{inl}(a)=\operatorname{record}_n=\mathrm{inl}(b)\Longrightarrow a=b.','      · -- The stored record','\nend\n')
]
assert ''.join(x['lean'] for x in steps)==s[body:s.index('\nend\n',body)].rstrip()+'\n'

